                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 22,
                            "last_played": 1789521416
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "When I was a young buck, this game was proclaimed a \"niche gem\". Now, I can gladly confirm that I can play this amazing game at my local Wendy's located in Wisconsin on my prestigious Steam Deck Model 102ZX. There've been instances in the past where people have told me \"because you are unable to play this game, you are to kid to play this legendary game. grow up kid!\". Well, here I am fellas. 20 years in the making and I can confidently proclaim that this game sucks. The only thing going for this niche gem (or should I say, \"niche Burger King\") is the cute fairy that flies around your screen. It reminded me of Paimon from Genshin Impact, but then it occurred to me that I actually hate Paimon from Genshin Impact. The fairy is actually the main antagonist of Pixel Puzzle 2: Anime, with her revealing her final/true form during the final puzzle, where you must deconstruct the puzzle in order for her to finally die. \n\n8/10, it has a little something for everyone",
